For me the limit in chess was my own skills.  If I'd played in
enough tourneys to have gotten a numerical rating it would have
been in the 1000-1100 range.  Quite mediocre.  I lost interest
when I realized that further efforts at some level weren't going to
improve my game any further.  It would have taken intense effort
and I might have only improved a few points.  From fodder at
tourneys to a player who does well without ever placing.  And
so my level of interest dropped because I had topped out.

For me the limit in Nethack is my own typos.  I can and do
keep getting better and better at the game play and it happens
at a level of effort that isn't heroic.  I haven't ascended in years
and the game evolves at a rate similar to my improvement.  And
so my level of interest remains.



